Ah, the old communist slogan! You know, I remember when I was a young whippersnapper, I used to think that was the bee's knees. And I still think it's a mighty fine idea, even at the ripe old age of 81. Now, I know some folks might say it's a recipe for disaster, that it's too utopian, too idealistic. But I think it's just common sense. Why should those who have more than they need be hoarding it all to themselves? And why should those who are struggling to get by have to suffer because they can't afford the basics?

