In Korea, we have a strong emphasis on education and socialization, and I believe that this is key to raising well-behaved and well-adjusted children. By providing a nurturing environment, offering guidance and support, and modeling good behavior ourselves, we can help our children develop into responsible and respectful individuals. So, in my opinion, good parents should not spank their children, but rather use alternative methods that prioritize love, understanding, and mutual respect." }

